ing jurisdiction in the country, with a partisan lean of 44 points toward Democrats. No incumbent is on the ballot, and no candidate-level polling or expert ratings exist for this race, so the forecast rests on the district's overwhelming structural Democratic advantage. Democrats have carried DC in every presidential election, typically by enormous margins.\n\nWith no competitive dynamics in evidence, the race is rated Safe Democratic. The real uncertainty concerns the size of the margin rather than the winner, since Republican support in the district is minimal and no polling exists to pin down the exact split. Any surprise would require an unprecedented shift in the district's electorate, which has shown no sign of occurring.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9995, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 1.0, "margin": 44.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 1.0, "margin": 50.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9999, "margin": 50.0}]}